{
  "requirement": "For requirement and example evidence, both `true` and `FIXME` MUST satisfy the determination check in `habeas::validate()`. A false determination MUST fail validation and be reported with its rationale. Each definition's determination MUST be checked on its own; a false determination MUST NOT fail the definitions it implements, tests, or cites. All other evidence checks MUST still pass: FIXME MUST NOT excuse malformed, missing, or stale evidence or uncovered references. Validation MUST check the recorded outcome, schema, input freshness, and reference coverage without inference or reassessing whether a source comment adequately acknowledges a gap.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "**Implementation**\n\nThe `{impl}` marker sits on the determination check in `validate_evidence_file` (`src/evidence.rs`, around line 684).\n\n- `Judgment::from_value` (`src/judgment.rs`) parses the recorded outcome. It accepts `true`, `false`, or `{\"FIXME\": [nonempty strings]}` and rejects everything else. `true` and `FIXME` add no determination error, so both satisfy the check.\n- `determination == Some(Judgment::False)` pushes `\"<label>: determination is false: <trimmed rationale>\"` into `errors`. A false determination therefore fails validation and is reported with its rationale. The record's label scopes the error to that one record.\n- The error is attached only to the evidence file being validated. `validate_references` never consults the determination except for the separate example-test check, which belongs to another requirement. A false determination therefore does not fail the definitions that implement, test, or cite it.\n- Every other check in the same function still runs after the determination check: text freshness, schema, rationale, references digest, dependencies, and input freshness. `validate_references` also still runs coverage and reference-set checks. Nothing treats FIXME specially to skip them.\n- Validation reads only the recorded value. It never reads the source comments, so it makes no inference about whether a FIXME acknowledgement is adequate.\n- The `{impl}` code does nothing beyond what the requirement states. The other-concern code in `validate_evidence_file` carries its own `{impl}` markers for schema, reference_set, requirement_text and so on.\n\n**Tests**\n\n- `a_false_determination_fails_only_its_own_record_with_its_rationale` (`src/evidence.rs`) checks the exact error text with the trimmed rationale. It also checks that a requirement that is implemented and cited by the false one produces no error.\n- `collects_missing_orphan_format_false_and_changed_line_errors` checks that a false record still reports its text, input, and schema errors alongside `determination is false`.\n- `tests/commands.rs::fixme_fixture` validates FIXME requirements and examples with and without issue numbers, and asserts no errors.\n- `fixme_examples_pass_without_test_references_but_true_examples_do_not` and `fixme_requirements_accept_issue_references_and_other_content` (`tests/outcomes.rs`) show that `true` and `FIXME` pass. They also show that `false` fails with `determination is false`, and that a FIXME entry is accepted whether or not it is an issue reference.\n- `fixme_does_not_hide_stale_inputs_or_uncovered_references` shows that FIXME does not excuse stale inputs or uncovered `{impl}` references.\n- The `tests/authoring_batch.rs` tests round-trip true, false, and FIXME records through validation.\n\nThese tests cover the design space: true, false, FIXME, false isolation, and FIXME not masking other failures. I found no gaps and no FIXME acknowledgements.",
  "references": "ccb6c92faf3ef198762d0ad3f63f1b70960ce9f97e0e4a55ce3fd3bed1293d85",
